# Data. The Olist CSVs are third-party data under CC BY-NC-SA and are not redistributable from
# this repository; the generated ones are reproducible from a seed.
#
# THE WHOLE `data/` TREE, not `data/olist/*.csv`. The narrow pattern was what I had, and it failed
# the moment the download was unzipped one directory higher than expected - 164 MB of CSVs and a
# 44 MB archive.zip went into a commit. `git status` showed them as ordinary untracked files
# because they were, and `git add -A` took them.
#
# An ignore rule has to cover where files ACTUALLY land, not where the instructions said to put them.
data/**
!data/.gitkeep

# Benchmark datasets (Spider is ~100 MB, downloaded on demand)
eval/spider/database/
eval/spider/*.json
!eval/spider/.gitkeep

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# dev-stack.ps1 process logs
.logs/

# Evaluation reports: keep them, they are the evidence for the accuracy numbers.
# (They are small JSON and re-running costs an LLM budget, so they are worth committing.)

